/*
==================== runBlocking — COMPLETE THEORY ====================

1️⃣ What is runBlocking?

- A coroutine builder.
- Blocks the current thread.
- Waits until coroutine finishes.
- Returns the result of the coroutine block.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

2️⃣ Actual Signature

fun <T> runBlocking(block: suspend CoroutineScope.() -> T): T

It is generic.
It returns whatever the block returns.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

3️⃣ Two Usage Styles

A) With Return Type

val result = runBlocking {
    10 * 5
}

Return type = Int
result = 50

--------------------------------------------------

B) Without Return Type

runBlocking {
    println("Hello")
}

Return type = Unit

---------------------------------------------------------------------

4️⃣ Why Both Are Allowed?

Because runBlocking is generic.
If block returns value → runBlocking returns value.
If block returns nothing → return type is Unit.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

5️⃣ What Does Blocking Mean?

It blocks the current thread.
Next line will not execute until coroutine finishes.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

6️⃣ When To Use runBlocking?

✔ main() function
✔ Console apps
✔ Unit tests
✔ Bridging suspend functions

---------------------------------------------------------------------

7️⃣ When NOT To Use?

❌ Android UI thread
❌ Inside Activity
❌ Inside Composable
❌ Inside ViewModel

Use lifecycleScope or viewModelScope instead.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

8️⃣ runBlocking vs launch vs async

runBlocking → Blocks thread → Returns T
launch      → Non-blocking → Returns Job
async       → Non-blocking → Returns Deferred<T>

---------------------------------------------------------------------

🔑 ONE LINE SUMMARY

runBlocking blocks the current thread until coroutine completes
and returns the result of the coroutine block.

=======================================================================
*/
